As can be seen in this output:
All versions give a TRUE convergence value.
Only version 0.6-5 seems to truly find the absolute minimum (although it's possible that there was something wrong in this version that has been corrected?)
Version 0.6-6 and 0.6-7, although don't find the absolute minimum, give very similar values for the estimates of the parameters in conflict (but 0.6-7 is clearly far from the absolute minimum).
Only version 0.6-6 "warns" that the polyserial correlation of c3 with the sp variables has not converged (although the polyserial correlation values don't seem weird, see below).
Version 0.6-7 warns of a poliserial correlation close to 1.0 (which doesn't seem to be, see below).
>From version 0.6-8 on, the result is stable, with a warning about the negative covariances.

